c\n  architecture/handoff done-check (NOT graded on numeric fidelity).\n\n## Assumption map (premortem-derived; each has a mitigation in the phases)\n- A1 *gemini-cli reachable for cross-family judging* â†’ MITIGATED by capability-gated branch (deterministic-only fallback; never silent same-family). [serves NS2/NS3]\n- A2 *Foreman's test-gate substrate can host arbitrary canary suites* â†’ DERISKED by Phase-0 Wave 0 spike before any skill depends on it. [serves NS2]\n- A3 *the eval harness is reusable across 3 validator types (R6)* â†’ DERISKED by building it as ONE harness + three pluggable check modules in Phase-0. [serves NS2/NS5/NS6]\n- A4 *Gandalf-bootstrap (review engine reviewing itself)* â†’ BROKEN by gating Gandalf on deterministic canaries + cross-family judge built BEFORE it. [serves NS3]\n- A5 *\"architecture/handoff success\" is definable deterministically* â†’ LOCKED in Phase-1 design as a concrete checklist (handoff gates pass + firewall artifacts exist + recipe emits Assumptions Ledger + end-to-end run completes). [serves NS6]\n\n## Phases (the master sequence)\n\n> **Sizing note (Shark 1 BLOCKER):** breadth-first makes this a LARGE plan set. It remains ONE Foreman\n> plan set but is honestly multi-wave; Foreman auto-advances across waves with budget pre-flight + resume.\n> Phase 0 alone is ~6 waves; each cognitive skill is ~1â€“2 waves; the slice ~2. Stage 2 decomposes them.\n\n### Phase 0 â€” Shared infrastructure (FIRST; everything below depends on it) â€” ~6 waves\nThe cross-cutting machinery every skill wave reuses. Built ONCE, on the trio/Foreman substrate, Foundry\nstays stateless.\n- **P0.A Eval harness on Foreman substrate (R1/R2/R6) â€” opens with Wave-0 go/no-go spike (FIX-3):** the\n  spike proves a wrapped validator emits TAP/pytest PASS events the Foreman gate counts (not vacuous-green).\n  Go â‡’ build ONE harness + three validator modules ALL emitting TAP/pytest (FIX-1/4): (i) schema+path-existence\n  (handoff), (ii) deterministic + cross-family canary eval (sleep/no-regression), (iii) numeric-tolerance\n  grader (paper-repro). Cross-family judge via gemini-cli, capability-gated; FIX-7 fallback honesty.\n  No-go fallback: validators run as a standalone Node test process Foreman shells to. [NS2,NS5,NS6]\n- **P0.B Machine-checkable handoff contract (NS5):** formalize the contract schema (north_star round-trip,\n  artifact_refs existence-check, block-on-open-questions, versioned persisted artifact); wire it as the\n  reusable gate that Anchor's HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md + Crucible's locate-plan.mjs both emit/validate.\n- **P0.C Skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model table (NS1,NS3,NS4):** the per-skill repo skeleton â€”\n  NORTH-STAR.md (purpose + machine-checkable non-goals as negative tests, R4 + invariants), SKILL.md,\n  references/{journal-schema,improvement}.md, LESSONS.md, journal/ (append-only), CHANGELOG.md. Plus the\n  NET-NEW logical-tierâ†’model **config table** (the brain seam) + a **swap test** (FIX-5): swapping the table\n  changes the resolved model with zero skill-prose edits.\n- **P0.D Journal + sleep loop (NS1,NS2,NS3,R5):** the 7-field journal schema; the sleep meta-recipe\n  (clusterâ†’cross-context-corroborated distillâ†’North-Star gateâ†’eval-gateâ†’versioned promote w/ rollback).\n  Distillation requires cross-context corroboration, provenance-distrust of unverified entries (R5).\n- **P0.E Foundry governance wiring + canary versioning (FIX-6):** map.json entries + append-only invariant\n  tests so canary SETS and templates are recorded as data/refs (Foundry stays stateless prose-only); drift\n  checker stays GREEN. Canary sets are versioned ALONGSIDE skill versions; sleep may APPEND canaries, never\n  edit/delete (deletion = human call).\n- **P0.F Citation hygiene + provenance (R7):** correct SkillsBenchâ†’2602.12670, drop/replace MemoryGraft in\n  all carried docs; provenance fields in journal schema.\n\n### Phase 1 â€” Gandalf (critical review) â€” Wave 1 of the cognitive skills\nFirst skill, because it is also the Review-stage engine for later waves. Gated by P0 infra (A4 broken).\nPersona tier = top (Fable 5). Ships with its NORTH-STAR (non-goals as negative tests), a frozen canary set,\nand a seeded journal. [NS1,NS2,NS3,NS6]\n\n### Phase 2 â€” Ramanujan (math/algorithm understanding)\nBuilds the reasoning/algorithm graph the recipe's understandâ†’build firewall depends on. Tier = top. [NS6]\n\n### Phase 3 â€” Literature review (augmented researchPrime) â€” MOVED EARLY\nUpstream lineage/lit-review is load-bearing for paper-repro (recovers tacit knowledge). Tier = Opus. [NS6]\n\n### Phase 4 â€” Data analysis (find/clean/analyze/report)\nData pipeline + result comparison for the reproduction. Tier = Sonnetâ†’Opus. [NS6]\n\n### Phase 5 â€” Analytic + ML code (R/Matlab/Python; JAX/PyTorch) + Code verification (CO-DESIGNED)\nCode generation/execution AND the fidelity firewall, designed together (code-verification is not bolted on\nlast). Understandâ†’build firewall: frozen algorithm spec + unit tests from Ramanujan gate the code. Verify on\nEXECUTED numbers w/ tolerance. Tier = Opus / Fable 5 for verification. [NS5,NS6]\n\n### Phase 6 â€” recreate-a-paper recipe (THE SLICE / PROOF)\nComposes Phases 1â€“5. Required upstream lineage/lit-review; explicit Assumptions Ledger for tacit gaps;\nunderstandâ†’build firewall; executed-number verification BOUND to the firewall module (FIX-8); context-isolated\ncross-family grader (ADVISORY, FIX-15). GRADED on the deterministic architecture/handoff done-check (A5),\nreproducing Gelman ANOVA. [NS5,NS6 â€” the proof]\n\n### Phase 7 â€” NS1 self-improvement demonstration (the self-improving proof) â€” ~1 wave\nHomes FIX-13. Depends on: â‰¥1 built skill (Phase 1+) with its genuine-execution journal + the P0.D sleep loop.\nInject a KNOWN defect (a seeded regression failing â‰¥1 named canary) into the chosen skill; run a real sleep\ncycle (clusterâ†’distillâ†’North-Star gateâ†’eval gateâ†’versioned promote);