{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01A3obgZxrMGorReic7ebrL4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the grounding I need from the Master Plan and the Stage-0 Intake. Here is the summary.\n\n## Portfolio Program â€” Master Plan (Crucible Stage 1): Grounded Summary\n\n**Locked North Star & frame**\n- The program builds a deep, self-improving, **model-agnostic** skill repository in Skill Foundry â€” cognitive skills, compositional recipes, later stateful agents â€” where every skill carries a LOCKED North Star, journals its own real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\" sessions *without drifting* from its designed purpose.\n- The **first end-to-end proof** is a `recreate-a-paper` recipe reproducing the **Gelman ANOVA** paper, graded on **architecture/handoff success â€” not numeric reproduction fidelity**. Extend-own-work is explicitly the *second* slice.\n- This Master Plan is **one Foreman-ready plan set**, executed as sequential per-skill wave-groups whose first executable wave is Phase-0 shared infrastructure.\n\n**Stage-1 convergence outcome (2026-06-20)**\n- The Shark-Tank found **3 â‰¥2-agree BLOCKERs + 2 MAJORs**. The scope fork was resolved by the user (convergence authority) as **BREADTH-FIRST**: build all five cognitive skills to production depth (full canary sets + journals) *before* the recreate-a-paper slice.\n- Convergence took **multiple rounds**: v2 (initial fixes), then a substrate-verified **round 2 (v3)** that found v2's gate \"sound in plumbing but unsound in semantics,\" plus **v4-hardening** on FIX-8 and FIX-13.\n\n**The governing semantic fix (PRINCIPLE-D)**\n- The no-regression GATE emits TAP `ok`/`not ok` **only from deterministic checks** (numeric tolerance, code/unit tests, path/schema existence). **LLM-judge and cross-family judging are ADVISORY** â€” recorded as report artifacts, never emitting a gate verdict.\n- Rationale captured: a non-deterministic judge could otherwise flip the gate GREENâ†”HALT, and an unreachable cross-family host could otherwise HALT the build; since Foreman HALT is terminal, judging must stay *out* of the gate path. This explicitly **corrects the earlier (v2) FIX-7** which wrongly allowed a HALT-on-unreachable-host.\n\n**Anti-gameability of the proof**\n- **FIX-8 (anti-fabrication floor):** the slice's emitted statistic is **bound** to the firewall-verified module's output on the same input (tolerance-identical), plus a deterministic perturbation test. The *binding* (not perturbation alone) defeats input-proportional fabrication. It does **not** grade fidelity (honors R3).\n- **FIX-10 / FIX-5:** firewall unit tests are emitted by Ramanujan in a context separate from and before the code that must satisfy them; the tierâ†’model swap test asserts model change with zero skill-prose edits.\n\n**NS1 is gated, not asserted**\n- **FIX-13** homes NS1 in its own **Phase 7** as **regression-then-recovery** (not mere \"non-decrease\"): inject a known seeded defect failing â‰¥1 named canary, run a real sleep cycle, and require that canary to *recover to passing* while all prior canaries stay green â€” a no-op/rollback revision cannot pass.\n- **FIX-14:** the NS1 demo distills **only** from genuine-execution-provenance journal entries (captured from real dogfood/canary runs, not fabricated prose), so the proof is non-circular and honors R5 provenance-distrust.\n\n**Per-skill cadence correction (FIX-12)**\n- Corrected on 2026-06-20: the program is **not** one monolithic Foreman plan building thin skills. Only **Phase 0** is the immediate Foreman plan; **each cognitive skill is its own researchPrime â†’ skill-Crucible â†’ Foreman â†’ Learn cycle** so the best-in-class *method* (not just a structural done-floor) is researched per skill. (Program sequence lives in `PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`.)\n\n**Phase sequence (the master ordering)**\n- **Phase 0** (~6 waves, FIRST, hard dependency): eval harness on Foreman substrate opening with a Wave-0 go/no-go spike (P0.A); machine-checkable handoff contract (P0.B); skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model table with swap test (P0.C); journal + sleep loop (P0.D); Foundry governance + append-only canary versioning (P0.E); citation hygiene/provenance (P0.F).\n- **Phases 1â€“5** (cognitive skills, ~1â€“2 waves each): Gandalf (critical review, first because it's the later Review engine; A4 self-review bootstrap broken), Ramanujan (math/algorithm), Literature review (moved early), Data analysis, Analytic+ML code **co-designed with** code verification.\n- **Phase 6**: the recreate-a-paper slice (composes 1â€“5). **Phase 7**: the NS1 self-improvement demonstration.\n\n**Per-skill \"DONE\" floor (TAP-gated)**\n- A skill wave-group is done iff: `NORTH-STAR.md` with â‰¥3 machine-checkable non-goals as negative canaries; a frozen set of â‰¥K deterministic canaries covering core capability + every non-goal; a `journal/` of â‰¥M genuine-execution fixture entries in the 7-field schema; and all P0 gates GREEN + `map.json` registered. (K and M set per-skill at Stage 2.)\n\n**Carried resolutions & assumptions**\n- R1â€“R7 from the intake are folded in as plan items: real eval-gate host (reuse Foreman's Node orchestrator), cross-family+deterministic verification, slice graded on architecture/handoff, machine-checkable non-goals, corroborated provenance-distrusting distillation, one harness/three validator types, and citation fixes (SkillsBench = arXiv 2602.12670; drop/replace MemoryGraft).\n- Five premortem assumptions (A1â€“A5) each have a homed mitigation â€” notably A2 (substrate can host canary suites) derisked by the P0 Wave-0 spike, and A4 (self-reviewing review engine) broken by gating Gandalf on deterministic canaries + a cross-family judge built before it.\n\n**Explicit out-of-scope (anti-drift)**\n- GWL harness / t2rs brain (parallel track), stateful productivity/personal agents (later phases), and the extend-own-paper second slice.\n\n**Note on grounding:** every claim above is sourced from `crucible/MASTER-PLAN.md` and `CRUCIBLE-INTAKE.md`. I did not open `PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`, `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`, or the Phase-0 research run â€” flag if you want those cross-checked or the per-skill K/M (Stage-2) values pulled in."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10376,"cache_read_input_tokens":29256,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10376},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b76639d-e7e8-4d78-8080-49add8f1412a","uuid":"27b35016-7027-4278-b694-c4c43538f415","request_id":"req_011CcFSSw427ZLwufUUFGyoz"}
